From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: build TinyUSB 0.21 on the P4, keep 0.18 on the S2/S3.

The esp32 port builds TinyUSB from the espressif/tinyusb managed
component, pinned to micropython/tinyusb-espressif's
cherrypick/dwc2_zlp_fix branch: TinyUSB 0.18 plus the DWC2 OUT-endpoint
ZLP fix (hathach/tinyusb#3154, fixed by #3293). This keeps that source
and picks a ref per target with the component manager's `matches`
list: the ESP32-P4 takes v0.21.0.1-micropython1, the S2 and S3 keep the
cherry-pick, and every other target still gets no TinyUSB.

v0.21.0.1-micropython1 is MicroPython's own tag in the same fork:
espressif/tinyusb 0.21.0~1 plus Damien George's "don't flush pending
data in cdcd_open" (hathach/tinyusb#3807). It carries the ZLP fix
("short packet (including ZLP when byte_count == 0)" in dcd_dwc2.c).
Against the registry's 0.21.0~2 it lacks only a DWC2 periodic-transfer
option that is off by default and an NCM divisor change, neither of
which this port uses. A registry version would need a second source,
and one dependency can only have one.

What this changes for a USB audio device on the P4: from 0.19 the audio
class finishes an isochronous OUT packet in the USB interrupt
(audiod_xfer_isr): it copies the packet into the endpoint FIFO, re-arms
the endpoint and calls tud_audio_rx_done_isr(). In 0.18 all of that
waited for tud_task(), which on this port runs in the MicroPython task
through the scheduler, so a busy interpreter left the endpoint unarmed
and lost packets. Measured on an ESP32-P4 sound card (usbif) with the
interpreter allocating in a tight loop: 91-95 % of packets delivered
on 0.18, heard as a tick every few tens of milliseconds.

Why not the S3 as well, for now: on a LILYGO T-Embed (ESP32-S3, full
speed) espressif's 0.21.0~1 and ~2 enumerate, but the moment the host
opens the CDC port the chip trips the interrupt watchdog inside the
DWC2 IN-endpoint handler (dcd_int_handler -> handle_ep_irq, dir IN) and
reboots. The one commit v0.21.0.1-micropython1 adds, hathach/tinyusb
#3808's "don't flush pending data in cdcd_open", fixes it: on that tag
the S3 opens its port and runs normally. Moving the S2 and S3 is a
separate change (usbif#48); until then they stay where upstream has
them.

The API changes that reach a user C module are 0.19's and 0.20's:
tud_audio_rx_done_post_read_cb() became tud_audio_rx_done_isr() and
runs in the ISR, and TUD_AUDIO_EP_SIZE() takes the bus speed as its
first argument. Nothing in MicroPython itself uses either. A module
that builds for both chips now sees both versions, so it guards on
TUSB_VERSION_NUMBER.

One behaviour change to know about: 0.21's DWC2 driver arms an
isochronous OUT endpoint for the microframe after the current one,
whatever its interval (0.18 did that only for bInterval 1). A
high-speed isochronous OUT endpoint with a longer interval then waits
on the wrong frame parity and receives nothing; usbif's sound card at
bInterval 4 got no packets at all until it went back to 1, which the
interrupt-time re-arm makes safe.

The P4's lockfile is part of this patch, and only its TinyUSB entry
moves, to the tag's commit. The component manager re-solves when the
manifest changes, but it keeps a git commit it has already locked for
as long as the source is the same, and here the source is. Without the
lockfile change the P4 would quietly go on building 0.18. The other
targets' lockfiles keep the cherry-pick commit they already hold.
---
diff --git a/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml b/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
index ddd7cb2..15a481f 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
+++ b/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
@@ -3,12 +3,21 @@ dependencies:
   # resource usage
   espressif/mdns: "~1.3.0"
   espressif/tinyusb:
-    rules:
-      - if: "target in [esp32s2, esp32s3, esp32p4]"
-    # Temporary workaround for https://github.com/hathach/tinyusb/issues/3154
-    # Can be removed once fix is released in espressif/tinyusb
+    # One source, a ref per target. The P4 takes TinyUSB 0.21 (MicroPython's
+    # own v0.21.0.1-micropython1 tag), which re-arms the audio class's
+    # isochronous OUT endpoint in the ISR, not in tud_task(). The S2 and S3
+    # stay on the 0.18 cherry-pick for now (usbif#48: espressif's 0.21.0~2
+    # resets an S3 when the host opens the CDC port; this tag does not).
+    # The first matching `if` picks the ref; a target that matches none
+    # (esp32, the C-series) gets no TinyUSB, as before.
     git: https://github.com/micropython/tinyusb-espressif.git
-    version: cherrypick/dwc2_zlp_fix
+    matches:
+      - if: "target == esp32p4"
+        version: v0.21.0.1-micropython1
+      # Temporary workaround for https://github.com/hathach/tinyusb/issues/3154
+      # Can be removed once fix is released in espressif/tinyusb
+      - if: "target in [esp32s2, esp32s3]"
+        version: cherrypick/dwc2_zlp_fix
   espressif/esp_hosted:
     rules:
       - if: "target == esp32p4"
diff --git a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4 b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4
index a338b20..cc6e557 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4
+++ b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ dependencies:
       type: service
     version: 1.3.2
   espressif/tinyusb:
-    component_hash: ee1c962cff61eb975d508258d509974d58031cc27ff0d6c4117a67a613a49594
+    component_hash: b8cf4577c72e77dcc180f2fd46fe6ea9883190e389c5fe90504a47908ae02637
     dependencies:
     - name: idf
       version: '>=5.0'
@@ -77,7 +77,8 @@ dependencies:
     - esp32s3
     - esp32p4
     - esp32h4
-    version: e4c0ec3caab3d9c25374de7047653b9ced8f14ff
+    - esp32s31
+    version: 5c5c660317943820d49ce5c188f1bd60cd8aade6
   idf:
     source:
       type: idf
